actions:
- took H90 (user-reported red CI) ahead of the cycle-11 SE review; told the
  in-flight SE subagent to allocate from H91 so the IDs do not collide.
- reproduced the failure: CI `claims_check --count-check` prints
  `count mismatches: 9`; local is 0. A depth-1 clone prints 9, the same SHA
  with full history prints 0 -> the checkout, not the ledger.
- root cause: actions/checkout@v4 defaults to fetch-depth 1; `_exp_revision`
  then sees only the tip, so every claim is pinned to the tip and old selftest
  counts are compared with today's tools.
- fix: fetch-depth 0 in ci.yml (pack 3.2 MiB, 809 commits) + history_is_shallow
  in claims_check (skip the rule in a shallow tree, print why; H78's own
  "no measurement revision" rule). C-4015's quoted count 25->28.
- first PR run still red: my own C-4136 shared a cell with tools/gate.py, so
  the rule attributed 28 to gate.py (11). Split into one tool per claim
  (C-4137 gate.py, C-4138 the re-pin), pushed, CI green.
- navigator round 1: APPROVE, with two non-blocking number flags (the red run
  is 12 consecutive pushes 1889340..2b3d1b4, last green 3f9c0b2; the depth-1
  recipe must pin the pre-fix tool revision). Both fixed before merge.
- wrote prompt_qa.txt (Check the runs: report red/cancelled main runs since
  the last pass, each with SHA + failing step, give each a task; "green
  locally" is not green in CI) and prompt_tl.txt (`gh pr checks <n>` before
  merging a PR).
- merged #210 (47ebf18); CI on main success at 47ebf18.

decisions:
- fetch-depth 0 rather than an allow-list: the rule is only meaningful with
  history, and 3 MiB is cheap. Allowing the 9 mismatches would have hidden the
  next real one.
- skip-with-a-message rather than "0 mismatches" in a shallow tree: a SKIP is
  never a pass, and the number must never look checked when it was not.
- H90 ahead of the SE review: user-visible red CI on the default branch beats
  process order; the SE subagent ran in parallel and left H90 untouched.

